## Project Overview

Keeping operating systems up to date is one of the most important responsibilities of a System Administrator or DevOps Engineer. Security vulnerabilities, bug fixes, and operating system improvements are released frequently by Linux and Windows vendors. Manually logging into every server to install updates becomes difficult, time-consuming, and error-prone as the number of servers grows.

**AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager** solves this problem by allowing administrators to automate the process of scanning, approving, scheduling, and installing operating system patches across Amazon EC2 instances.

This repository documents the complete hands-on implementation of Patch Manager on an Ubuntu EC2 instance. Every configuration, command, troubleshooting step, and explanation is included so that even a beginner can reproduce the same setup.

---

# Project Objectives

The objectives of this project are to:

- Configure AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager
- Understand Patch Baselines
- Configure Patch Policies
- Configure Maintenance Windows
- Register Managed Instances
- Execute Patch Operations
- Verify Patch Compliance
- Troubleshoot Patch Manager failures
- Understand the IAM permissions required for Patch Manager

